  "body": "What happens: the `release.yml` run for tag `v0.19.0` (run 43452818098) failed in two jobs, so the published release carries only the Windows zip, the Windows installer and the FreeBSD tarball. v0.18.0 carried twelve assets (AppImage, deb, rpm, flatpak, snap, tar.gz, Arch package, macOS dmg and zip as well).\n\n- `linux`, step \"Assemble Linux packages\" (`scripts/package-linux.sh`): `install: cannot stat 'assets/ui/cube.png': No such file or directory`\n- `macos`, step \"Assemble macOS app and disk image\": `Warning: assets/ui/cube.png not a valid file - skipping` (ten times), then `CamCraft.iconset:Failed to generate ICNS.`\n- `aur`, `flatpak`, `snap` were skipped because `linux` failed.\n- `windows`, `freebsd`, `wasm`, `site`, `publish`, `pages` are green.\n\nExpected: the packaging scripts find the app icon, and a release has the same asset set as v0.18.0.\n\nEvidence: both scripts read `assets/ui/cube.png`; the file is not in the tree tagged `v0.19.0` (it was there for v0.18.0, whose run built all packages). Something merged between the two tags removed or renamed it. The local release gate does not run the Linux or macOS packaging scripts, so the cut did not see it.\n\nTo find: which commit removed or renamed the file (`git log --diff-filter=DR --name-status v0.18.0..v0.19.0 -- assets/ui/cube.png`), and every other reader of that path (`scripts/package-*.sh`, Flatpak/Snap/AUR manifests, the site).\n\nDone means: the packaging scripts point at an icon that exists (or the icon is restored), a check that runs in the batch or release gate tier on any OS fails when a file the packaging scripts install is missing from the tree, and the next tag's `linux` and `macos` jobs are green. Whether 0.19.0 itself gets Linux and macOS packages (the tag is never moved) is the maintainer's decision.\n",
